    {
        "id": 3,
        "title": "Why 'Eon'?",
        "date": "Oct 15, 2025",
        "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1487958449943-2429e8be8625?q=80&w=1500&auto=format&fit=crop",
        "excerpt": "Design shouldn't be disposable. I named my practice \"Eon\" to serve as a constant reminder: Ignore the trends. Build systems that last.",
        "content": "\n            <p class=\"mb-6 text-lg font-medium text-white\">We are living in the era of \"Fast Design.\" It mimics the fashion industry—trends cycle every six months. A visual style that goes viral on TikTok today looks outdated and \"cringe\" by next month.</p>\n                <p class=\"mb-4\">For a business, chasing these trends is a dangerous financial game. It forces you to rebrand constantly just to stay relevant. It dilutes your identity. I established <strong>Eon Designs</strong> to reject this cycle entirely.</p>\n                <h3 class=\"text-white font-display text-2xl mt-10 mb-4\">The Geological Perspective</h3>\n                <p class=\"mb-4\">My background is unique in the design world. I am an engineering student. Specifically, Geological Engineering. In geology, we study time on a scale that is hard for humans to comprehend. An <strong>Eon</strong> is the largest division of geological time—spanning half a billion years or more.</p>\n                <p class=\"mb-4\">This concept is the cornerstone of my design philosophy. When you look at a rock formation, it stands because it has structure, stratification, and a solid foundation. It withstands the weather. Branding should be no different.</p>\n                <h3 class=\"text-white font-display text-2xl mt-10 mb-4\">Building Legacies, Not Posts</h3>\n                <p class=\"mb-4\">When I work with a client, I am not asking, \"What looks cool right now?\" I am asking, \"Will this visual system still work in ten years?\"</p>\n                <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 mb-6 space-y-3 marker:text-brand-500 text-gray-400\">\n                    <li><strong>Trends are like Weather:</strong> They change every day (Gradients, 3D icons, Brutalism).</li>\n                    <li><strong>Style is like Climate:</strong> It lasts for a season or a decade.</li>\n                    <li><strong>Principles are Geology:</strong> They last forever (Balance, Contrast, Hierarchy, Grid Systems).</li>\n                </ul>\n                <p class=\"mb-4\">I focus on the geology. I build systems based on mathematical grids and optical balance. That is the Eon promise: Design that is engineered to survive the test of time.</p>\n        "
    }
